summary.text:
Let me write the FB.

Logic: if Trip or !Request or invalid -> Count=0, Ready=FALSE. Else Count = min(qCount+1, Preset); Ready = (Count >= Preset).

Note P3: Ready <-> (Count >= Preset and valid). In invalid case Count=0 so false anyway.

Implementation straightforward.

Declaration:
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
 Request : BOOL;
 Trip : BOOL;
 Preset : USINT;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
 Ready : BOOL;
 Count : USINT;
END_VAR
VAR
END_VAR

Implementation:
IF Trip OR NOT Request OR (Preset < 1) OR (Preset > 5) THEN
    Count := 0;
    Ready := FALSE;
ELSE
    IF Count < Preset THEN
        Count := Count + 1;
    END_IF
    Ready := (Count >= Preset);
END_IF

Careful: Count is output, retained. But reading Count at scan start gives pre-state. Fine. Note if Count > Preset (shouldn't happen), no increment, Ready true. Fine.

USINT comparison with literal 1 fine.

Compile.

